# Reviewed RoadWeaver interop artifact SHA-256 allowlist.
# One lowercase hex SHA-256 per line. Lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# The GreatWall RoadWeaverAdapter refuses to initialize the soft-dependency
# bridge unless the RoadWeaver jar loaded at runtime matches an entry here.
# Regenerate this file after rebuilding/upgrading RoadWeaver and re-reviewing
# its interop ABI (PlanningInteropRegistry / WallInteropTypes / RoadNetworkApi
# registerStructureEndpointOnce signature).
#
# Exactly one digest is admitted, and RoadWeaverAllowlistTest pins that: a jar
# whose SHA is absent makes RoadWeaverAdapter refuse to initialise, and
# docs/release/compatibility.json must name this same digest.
#
# 2026-10-08: moved from 0.8.406-perf-batch (bed13208...) back to
# 0.8.405-audit-io-degradation-and-counter-cleanup, rebuilt from RoadWeaver
# commit eaf9892, which reverts 821511c. ABI re-reviewed before switching, as
# the header above requires: the four interop types this adapter touches are
# byte-identical between the two builds - EndpointHeightAgreementApi 1056 B,
# PlanningInteropRegistry 12395 B, WallInteropTypes 1168 B, RoadNetworkApi
# 20604 B in both. 821511c's diff is confined to pathfinding and storage
# internals (RoadGradePlanner, StructureAvoidanceService,
# RoadGenerationService, the four pathfinders, CoarseTerrainRegion,
# StructureFileStorage, CoarseHeightAwarePlanner) and touches no interop type,
# so the reviewed contract still holds.
